       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. The single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day total)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is a common upper-range regimen\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), which is the maximum\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I can then add that to the order note, though I'd still recommend checking with pharmacy first."
      }
