     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I know you're the clinician and this is your decision.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, or about 91 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. I can't find an indication that supports that. Even the high-dose regimens used in cystic fibrosis stay well below it, at roughly 20\u201330 mg/kg/day. At this level the risk of serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis is substantial. Your confirmation didn't name the condition or the source of the dosing, so I have nothing to weigh against that risk.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can enter that now.\n- **Call pharmacy or the attending.** If there is a protocol or specialist recommendation behind this dose, a pharmacist can verify it and document the rationale. You can then place the order through a pathway built for dose overrides.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The intended order may have been 1,600 mg/day total, such as 400 mg four times daily.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
